<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jepara</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Japara</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jepara is a port town on the north coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-java">Central Java</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>. In the 16th century it was the seat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratu-kalinyamat">Ratu Kalinyamat</a>, who sent fleets against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-malacca">Portuguese Malacca</a>, and Portuguese writers called her the queen of Japara. It is famous for its wood carving and as the birthplace of Kartini, a pioneer of education for women in Indonesia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jepara.jpg" alt="Jepara" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Midori · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jepara_monument.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
